{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00769",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.89,
      "end_seconds": 12.74,
      "duration_seconds": 11.85,
      "text": "Morning! It's my hands again. The arthritis. It flared up, since the cold weather started, and I'm back to square one."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 13.94,
      "end_seconds": 19.59,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "I'm sorry to hear that. Which joints, and how bad?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.54,
      "end_seconds": 33.86,
      "duration_seconds": 11.32,
      "text": "The knuckles and the base of my thumbs, both hands. Stiff and sore, especially in the morning. I can't open jars."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 36.49,
      "end_seconds": 40.68,
      "duration_seconds": 4.19,
      "text": "How long does the morning stiffness last?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 43.64,
      "end_seconds": 50.94,
      "duration_seconds": 7.3,
      "text": "An hour, an hour and a half. It was ten minutes in the summer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 54.16,
      "end_seconds": 58.04,
      "duration_seconds": 3.88,
      "text": "Any swelling or redness, or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 59.89,
      "end_seconds": 65.52,
      "duration_seconds": 5.63,
      "text": "A bit of swelling in the knuckles. No redness. No fever."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.67,
      "end_seconds": 74.1,
      "duration_seconds": 5.43,
      "text": "Any pain in other joints, like your knees, hips or spine?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 76.2,
      "end_seconds": 81.02,
      "duration_seconds": 4.82,
      "text": "No, my knees are okay. Just the hands."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 83.93,
      "end_seconds": 86.72,
      "duration_seconds": 2.79,
      "text": "Any rash or dry eyes?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 88.99,
      "end_seconds": 93.11,
      "duration_seconds": 4.12,
      "text": "No rash. My eyes are fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 94.21,
      "end_seconds": 101.93,
      "duration_seconds": 7.72,
      "text": "What are you taking, and how did the treatment go after our last visit?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 105.03,
      "end_seconds": 117.97,
      "duration_seconds": 12.94,
      "text": "A gel for the thumbs, I can't remember the name, I got it from the pharmacy. And naproxen, maybe 250 mg, twice a day, on and off."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.59,
      "end_seconds": 131.78,
      "duration_seconds": 12.19,
      "text": "So the gel you can't name, and naproxen 250 mg twice a day as you recall it. Any other history?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.82,
      "end_seconds": 141.24,
      "duration_seconds": 7.42,
      "text": "Osteoarthritis diagnosed years ago, and I had a stomach ulcer once."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 143.09,
      "end_seconds": 146.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.75,
      "text": "Do you have any allergies?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 149.85,
      "end_seconds": 156.22,
      "duration_seconds": 6.37,
      "text": "Years ago, a rash from penicillin, but I've avoided it ever since."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 159.2,
      "end_seconds": 169.3,
      "duration_seconds": 10.1,
      "text": "Thank you. Let me look at your hands. Put them on the table, palms down. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.05,
      "end_seconds": 189.16,
      "duration_seconds": 1.11,
      "text": "Here."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 191.3,
      "end_seconds": 203.12,
      "duration_seconds": 11.82,
      "text": "There's bony swelling of the end joints and the base of both thumbs, and tenderness with a bit of warmth in two knuckles, no redness."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 204.52,
      "end_seconds": 207.78,
      "duration_seconds": 3.26,
      "text": "Is it getting worse? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 209.31,
      "end_seconds": 225.16,
      "duration_seconds": 15.85,
      "text": "It's an osteoarthritis flare, as you say, but with the long morning stiffness and warm knuckles, I can't rule out an inflammatory arthritis, such as rheumatoid, on top of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 226.95,
      "end_seconds": 229.26,
      "duration_seconds": 2.31,
      "text": "Rheumatoid! Oh no. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 231.07,
      "end_seconds": 243.92,
      "duration_seconds": 12.85,
      "text": "It's a possibility, not a diagnosis. The key difference is the length of the morning stiffness, which is over an hour for you. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 246.38,
      "end_seconds": 249.71,
      "duration_seconds": 3.33,
      "text": "What do we do? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 252.56,
      "end_seconds": 261.45,
      "duration_seconds": 8.89,
      "text": "Keep using the gel, warm your hands in the morning, and wear thin gloves in cold weather."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 264.2,
      "end_seconds": 267.77,
      "duration_seconds": 3.57,
      "text": "I always forget gloves. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 270.84,
      "end_seconds": 278.23,
      "duration_seconds": 7.39,
      "text": "Put a pair by the front door. And take the naproxen with food only."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 280.13,
      "end_seconds": 281.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.34,
      "text": "Right. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 284.59,
      "end_seconds": 299.7,
      "duration_seconds": 15.11,
      "text": "If the knuckle swelling gets worse, you get new swelling in other joints, or the stiffness lasts all morning, come back to see me and I'll arrange blood tests and a referral."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.29,
      "end_seconds": 306.03,
      "duration_seconds": 3.74,
      "text": "I will. Thanks, doctor. ~"
    }
  ]
}
